{"Concurrent index builds lack per-key singleflight coalescing - narrowed lock scope allows multiple goroutines to redundantly build the same index with only last write winning cache assignment": 0.7705395221710205, "Skipping PostgreSQL test reduces CI coverage for the initialization path being changed - need tracked issue to fix and consider quarantined/flaky test approach instead of skipping entirely": 0.5519062876701355, "Moving Init to constructor is a significant behavioral change - constructor now performs expensive operations (index building) and can fail during startup rather than deferring to first request": 0.7166858911514282, "Calling code may not handle constructor failures appropriately after Init moved to constructor": 0.14498676359653473, "Deployment infrastructure may not account for potentially long startup times from eager initialization": 0.07036102563142776, "Possible circular dependencies that relied on lazy initialization may break with eager initialization": 0.05013955011963844, "Missing documentation of initialization contract change for future maintainers": 0.023972800001502037, "Initialization order reversed - search index now initializes before watcher starts, creating window where events could occur between index completion and watcher startup leading to potential index inconsistency": 0.6513723731040955, "Missing comment explaining safety guarantees of the new initialization ordering (e.g., full rebuild on startup or watch stream replay)": 0.38736042380332947}